<sn><md>### Amino Acid Classification

+++ read

| Category | Count | Amino Acids | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Essential Amino Acids** | 10 | Lysine, Valine, Isoleucine, Threonine, Tryptophan, Histidine, Arginine, Leucine, Methionine, Phenylalanine | Cannot be synthesized by the body; must be obtained through diet. Mnemonic: **L VITTAL MP** |
| **Semi-Essential Amino Acids** | 2 | Arginine, Histidine | Required in higher amounts during specific developmental stages (e.g., infancy). |
| **Non-Essential Amino Acids** | 10 | Alanine, Glycine, Cysteine, Asparagine, Glutamine, Tyrosine, Proline, Glutamic acid, Aspartic acid, Serine | Can be synthesized by the body; dietary intake is not mandatory. |

*Note: Arginine and Histidine appear in both the Essential and Semi-Essential categories depending on the classification system used.*


